Subject: [PATCH 02/13] Panchanga acquisition round 1: archive
 Uttaradi/SRS/Vishwesha, document gaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pulled all 14 APKs from the Drive folder and archived the Panchanga-bearing
ones as immutable source artifacts under dge/sources/, per the acquisition
architecture's manifest convention. Uttaradi and SRS are fully archived
structured sources; Vishwesha (Pejavara's Panchanga) is partial — its
five-anga daily data is packed in undecoded numeric codes, only the
festival/special-day annotations were recoverable as text.

Notable gaps recorded rather than glossed over: Udupi Panchanga's APK is
still missing from this delivery; Uttaradi/Tithi Nirnaya/Vyasaraja Sosale
all ship without any lib/ folder (no libapp.so for any ABI), so none of
the three can actually run or have their Dart logic inspected as supplied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
